sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747626000007/pep-20251227.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0019", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-27", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2877, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747626000007/pep-20251227.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0008", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-27", "section": "risk_factors", "score": 1.2695, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747626000007/pep-20251227.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10Q_2023-03-25__unknown__0013", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-03-25", "section": "unknown", "score": 0.54, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747623000023/pep-20230325.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10Q_2023-03-25__mdna__0031", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-03-25", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.0069, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747623000023/pep-20230325.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "PEP_10Q_2023-03-25__unknown__0012", "ticker": "PEP", "form": "10-Q", "fiscal_label": "Q1 FY2023", "period_end": "2023-03-25", "section": "unknown", "score": 0.0067, "filing_name": "PepsiCo Inc 10-Q Q1 FY2023", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/77476/000007747623000023/pep-20230325.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 23, "dropped_candidates": 254, "token_estimate": 31998, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "Both companies describe overlapping risk themes: shifting consumer preferences and health concerns, reputation damage, supply chain and input cost pressures, and changes in the retail landscape. Coca-Cola's 10-K for FY2024 (year ended December 31, 2024) uniquely stresses dependence on independent bottling partners [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020], while PepsiCo's 10-K for FY2025 (year ended December 27, 2025) names The Coca-Cola Company as its primary beverage competitor in many countries [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0005]. Both flag supply chain price volatility and tariffs [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0008] [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0010], and both flag product safety, health, and ingredient concerns that could reduce demand or bring regulation [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0014] [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0004]. The two filings cover different fiscal years, so differences may partly reflect timing; the filings do not rank their own risks, so no ranking is implied.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "KO", "company": "The Coca-Cola Company", "findings": [{"point": "The 10-K for FY2024 (ended December 31, 2024) says the company relies on independent bottling partners for a significant portion of its business, and that their decisions may not always align with Coca-Cola's interests.", "citations": ["KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It lists unfavorable economic and geopolitical conditions, including inflation and international conflicts, as a risk that could reduce demand and cause supply chain disruption.", "citations": ["KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0000", "KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0001"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It cites obesity and health-related concerns, potential taxes on sweetened beverages, and ingredient or packaging regulation as risks that may reduce demand for its beverages.", "citations": ["KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0012"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "PEP", "company": "PepsiCo Inc", "findings": [{"point": "The 10-K for FY2025 (ended December 27, 2025) cites shifting consumer preferences, including weight-loss drugs such as GLP-1 medications, tariffs and taxes, and private label switching, as factors that can reduce demand.", "citations": ["PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0001"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It states that The Coca-Cola Company is its primary beverage competitor in many countries, including the United States.", "citations": ["PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0005"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It describes cybersecurity incidents, reliance on third-party service providers, and ongoing enterprise-wide systems implementation as risks.", "citations": ["PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0016", "PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0019"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Theme", "Coca-Cola (10-K FY2024)", "PepsiCo (10-K FY2025)"], "rows": [["Consumer health concerns", "Obesity and health concerns may reduce demand [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0012]", "GLP-1 use, ingredient and processing concerns can reduce demand [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0001]"], ["Supply chain and input costs", "Price volatility; tariffs and inflation named [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0008]", "Price volatility; tariffs impacted supply chain [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0010]"], ["Retail landscape", "Retail consolidation, private label, e-commerce growth [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0003]", "E-commerce, hard discounters, private-label brands [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0008]"], ["Product safety and recalls", "Recalls possible; safety standards not always met [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0014]", "Recalls have occurred; inspections and fines possible [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0004]"], ["Distribution model", "Reliance on independent bottling partners [KO_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0020]", "Names Coca-Cola as primary beverage competitor [PEP_10K_2025-12-27__risk_factors__0005]"]]}, "citations"